  no dependencies.

  [1mMy recommendation: B.[0m The server is the only reliable place to record "who logged in." Since you're designing the
  backend contract from scratch anyway, putting it in [38;5;153m/login[39m costs nothing. Add [38;5;153m/events[39m when a second event type
  actually needs it. Pick [1mA[0m if you want the client to own tracking now, for example because the backend will be built
  much later or by another team.

[38;5;246m⏺ [39mUser answered Claude's questions:
[38;5;246m  ⎿  · Where should the login be recorded? → B: Server in /login (Recommended)[39m

[38;5;231m⏺[39m We'll go with B. Here's the first section of the design. I'll check with you after each one.

  [1mSection 1: Components and API contract[0m

  [1mAPI contract (new, documented in the spec):[0m
  - [38;5;153mPOST {API_BASE}/login[39m, body [38;5;153m{ username, password }[39m
    - [38;5;153m200[39m returns [38;5;153m{ userId: string }[39m. The server also stores a login record [38;5;153m{ userId, timestamp }[39m. That's the tracking.
    - [38;5;153m401[39m returns [38;5;153m{ error: string }[39m when the credentials are invalid.
  - [38;5;153mAPI_BASE = "https://api.example.com"[39m. The current [38;5;153mAPI_ENDPOINT[39m constant becomes this base URL.

  [1mClient modules (ES modules at the repo root, next to [38;5;153mapp.js[39m):[0m
  - [1m[38;5;153mapi.js[0m has [38;5;153mlogin(username, password)[39m. It makes a [38;5;153mfetch[39m POST and returns [38;5;153m{ userId }[39m, or throws on non-2xx or a
    malformed response. This file is the only one that knows URLs.
  - [1m[38;5;153msession.js[0m has [38;5;153msetUserId(id)[39m, [38;5;153mgetUserId()[39m (returns [38;5;153mnull[39m if unset) and [38;5;153mclearSession()[39m. It's the only file that
    touches [38;5;153msessionStorage[39m, under the key [38;5;153m"userId"[39m. Other forms will read the ID through [38;5;153mgetUserId()[39m.
  - [1m[38;5;153mapp.js[0m keeps [38;5;153mvalidateForm[39m and the submit handler. The handler becomes [38;5;153masync[39m. It calls [38;5;153mapi.login[39m, then
    [38;5;153msession.setUserId(result.userId)[39m on success, and shows an error on failure.
  - [1m[38;5;153mindex.html[0m changes to [38;5;153m<script type="module" src="app.js">[39m.

  [1mOut of scope:[0m logout UI, a real backend or mock server, [38;5;153m/events[39m, and token or cookie auth. [38;5;153mclearSession()[39m exists so a
  logout feature can use it later.

  Does this section look right? If so, next I'll cover the data flow and error handling.

